# Silicon Labs Project Configuration Tools: slcp, v0, Component selection file.
project_name: connect_bt_dmp_soc_light_cmsisos
label: connect_bt_dmp_soc_light_cmsisos
description: |
  The purpose of this application is to demonstrate simple wireless communication between two or more boards using the Connect SDK. When combined with the Connect-Switch sample application, it creates basic light functionality, allowing the LEDs to be toggled on the Light node. Upon power-up, the Light (acting as the network coordinator) creates its own local network. The Switch modules (low-power end-nodes) can then join this network and control the Light node. If a local network is established using the “form” CLI command, the Switch nodes can join using the “join” CLI command. From that point onward, the Light can be controlled by pressing the PB1 button on any connected Switch node.
category: Connect Examples
